GloomhavenVR @VERSION@ — how to install it
==========================================

Auf Deutsch: INSTALL-DEUTSCH.txt (liegt neben dieser Datei)

Play Gloomhaven (digital) as a room-scale VR board game: you stand at the table
and pick your cards up with your hands.

WHAT YOU NEED
  * Gloomhaven (digital) for PC, version 1.1.x — Steam or GOG.
  * Windows, and a PC-VR headset. Developed and tested on a Quest 3 over
    Virtual Desktop. Other headsets and streaming apps (Quest Link, Steam Link,
    SteamVR) should work, but have not been tested.
  * BepInEx 5.4.23.5 — a small, free program that lets mods run at all. You
    install it once. Step 1 below.

Everything else the mod needs is already inside this zip. Nothing else to
download.


1. INSTALL BepInEx, ONCE
   Download BepInEx_win_x64_5.4.23.5.zip from
     https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5
   and unpack it into your Gloomhaven folder — the folder with GH.exe in it.
   (On Steam: right-click the game -> Manage -> Browse local files.)

   Then start the game once the normal way and quit again. A new folder called
   BepInEx should now contain a file called LogOutput.log. That file appearing
   is your proof it worked.

2. INSTALL GloomhavenVR
   Unpack THIS zip into that same Gloomhaven folder and let Windows merge the
   BepInEx folder when it asks. To check it landed in the right place, look for
   these two folders:

     BepInEx\plugins\GloomhavenVR\
     BepInEx\patchers\GloomhavenVR\

   If either one is missing, unpack the zip again rather than moving files
   around by hand.

3. TELL YOUR HEADSET SOFTWARE TO HAND PC GAMES OVER
   Every headset has one setting that decides which app shows PC VR games. It is
   usually called the OpenXR runtime.
     Virtual Desktop  -> choose VDXR in the Virtual Desktop streamer settings.
     Quest Link       -> Meta Quest Link app, Settings, General, OpenXR Runtime,
                         "Set Meta Quest Link as active".
     Steam Link       -> SteamVR Settings, OpenXR, "Set SteamVR as OpenXR
                         runtime".

4. START THE GAME
   Put the headset on and start Gloomhaven the way you normally do.

   THE FIRST TIME YOU START IT AFTER INSTALLING OR UPDATING, THE GAME WILL CLOSE
   AND REOPEN BY ITSELF — ONCE. That is meant to happen. It is not a crash.
   See below.


WHY THE GAME RESTARTS ITSELF ONCE
---------------------------------
The mod switches on a speed setting that the game only reads while it is
starting up, so it can never take effect on the run that switches it on. Rather
than telling you to quit and start again, the mod does it for you.

On the test machine that setting was the difference between a stuttery 45 frames
per second and a smooth 90, and the smearing when you turn your head went away.

It happens once, after installing or updating. It cannot get stuck in a loop,
and it happens during start-up, before any save game is touched.

Don't want it? Open BepInEx\config\dev.gloomhavenvr.cfg and, under the [Core]
heading, set AutoRestartForGraphicsJobs = false. The game will then ask you to
restart it yourself instead.

This is the ONLY game file the mod ever changes: two lines added to
GH_Data\boot.config, everything else in it left alone, and the original saved
next to it as boot.config.gloomhavenvr-backup. If the game ever refuses to
start, copy that backup back over boot.config — the mod cannot fix that for you,
because at that point it never gets to run.


SETTINGS
--------
Everything is adjustable from inside the headset: open the game's own Options
window and pick the VR Options tab.

To play the game completely unmodified for a while, open
BepInEx\config\dev.gloomhavenvr.cfg and, under the [General] heading, set
Enabled = false. You do not have to uninstall anything.


PLAYING WITH OTHER PEOPLE
-------------------------
Everyone playing together needs the same version of the mod — if two people have
different versions, the game says so instead of letting the session go quietly
wrong. People without the mod at all can still play with you normally.


IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG
-----------------------
The game starts on your monitor instead of in the headset, or the headset stays
black? First check step 3 above. If that is right and it still happens, add
-force-d3d11 to the game's launch options in Steam or GOG.

Something else? There is one file to send, in your Gloomhaven folder:
  BepInEx\LogOutput.log
Send that whole file, say what you were doing, and say which headset you use and
how you connect it.

The full guide — playing, all the settings, known rough edges, uninstalling —
is the README on the project page:
  https://github.com/McFredward/GloomhavenVR
